    <meta name="atlas.prompt" content="The King's Chamber inside the Great Pyramid of Giza: a bare rectangular room built of huge polished red Aswan granite blocks in five wall courses with hairline joints, nine massive granite beams across the flat ceiling, a worn granite floor, one lidless dark granite sarcophagus standing near the west wall, a low square doorway in the corner of the north wall, lit by a few warm work lamps on the floor, dust in the air, documentary photograph, sharp focus"/>
    <meta name="atlas.grid" content="1280 720; fx = fy = 762.7223 px; cx 640, cy 360; pose camera-to-world, rub"/>
